  "output_text": "**Tax payable for FY 2026‑27 (new‑regime): ₹0.00**\n\n**Why the tax is zero**\n\n| Step (as shown by the calculator) | Figure | Explanation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Gross total income (salary) | ₹1,275,000.00 | Your stated earnings. |\n| Standard deduction (s. 16(ia) – FY 2026‑27) | ₹75,000.00 | The only deduction available in the new regime. |\n| **Taxable income** | **₹1,200,000.00** | Salary minus standard deduction. |\n| Tax on slabs (s. 115BAC) | ₹60,000.00 | Computed as 5 % on ₹4 L‑₹8 L (₹20,000) + 10 % on ₹8 L‑₹12 L (₹40,000). |\n| Rebate u/s 87A (income ≤ ₹12 L) | ₹60,000.00 | The rebate is the lesser of the tax payable (₹60,000) and the maximum rebate (₹60,000). |\n| Tax after rebate | ₹0.00 | ₹60,000 – ₹60,000 = ₹0.00. |\n| Health & Education Cess (4 % on tax) | ₹0.00 | No tax left to levy cess on. |\n| **Total tax liability** | **₹0.00** | No surcharge or other charges apply. |\n\nThus, under the **new tax regime** you owe **no income‑tax** for FY 2026‑27.\n\n---\n\n### Should you invest in ELSS?\n\n* **New‑regime deduction:** The new regime does **not** allow a deduction under Section 80C (which includes ELSS) — the only standard deduction is the ₹75,000 salary deduction already applied.\n* **Tax benefit:** Because the rebate under Section 87A already wipes out your tax liability, an ELSS investment would **not reduce your tax further** for this year.\n* **Other considerations:** ELSS can still be a good long‑term wealth‑creation tool (equity‑linked, 3‑year lock‑in), but the decision should be based on your investment goals, risk appetite, and portfolio diversification—not on immediate tax savings.\n\n---\n\n### Assumptions made\n\n1. **Only the standard deduction** (₹75,000) is claimed; no other deductions (e.g., 80D, 80G) are present.  \n2. The figures you provided are accurate and complete for FY 2026‑27.  \n3. You are electing the **new tax regime** (as stated).  \n\nIf you have other eligible deductions or are considering the **old regime**, the tax outcome could differ. Please share any additional exemption or deduction documents if you want a comparison.",
